  "worked_solution": "Since we have that \n\n$$\nP(x)⇔Q(x)≡(P(x)∧Q(x))∨(¬P(x)∧¬Q(x)),\n$$\n\n \n\nthe corresponding truth set can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P⇔Q}=({T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q})\\cup ({\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we sketch the set ${T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q}:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14114538/assets/c339e66441c947025f700d4206542e2a54bebf23b6973b835026170c8871eecf.png)\n\nThen, we sketch the set ${\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}$ and ${\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q}:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14114538/assets/5d0ea62a7e98b8383e436586cefd2065667eadd54caaa3006950add1c335a9ce.png)\n\nAs a result, ${\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q}$ is the following: \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14114538/assets/05873c0302db6dc55a078962f99da6a6dc9fa1dbbdd75b688e0f503277d66f1c.png)\n\nFinally, to get the truth set of $P(x)⇔Q(x),$ we take all the points that belong to ${T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q}$ or ${\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q}:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14114538/assets/a8aca0881a2d233f604ccf65721fb3ee8f1e2a4a1f0f58d361aca510a28c6ccb.png)",
